#opener("The PiForma was built to be used and carried, with a little care. Its case has already had a long life; the electronics inside would prefer a reasonably quiet one.")
#block(breakable:false)[
#heading(level:2,"Handling the computer and display")
#para("Use the carrying handle as described in Chapter 1 and watch the keyboard as the computer comes out of the bag. Avoid impacts, pressure on the display, and pulling on connected cables.")
#para("The display connections need gentle handling. Do not try to cure a flicker by tapping the case or moving internal parts while powered. Record the symptom and let the builder investigate.")
]
#block(breakable:false)[
#heading(level:2,"Keyboard and mouse care")
#para("Keep crumbs, liquids, and loose items out of the keys. Pack the keyboard with its keys toward the bag wall, thick edge rear, and thin edge front. Turn the mouse off for prolonged storage or transport if desired, and keep its receiver accounted for.")
]
#block(breakable:false)[
#heading(level:2,"Charging and storage")
#para("The owner prefers to keep the main battery above roughly 25–50% most of the time rather than repeatedly running it empty. This is a personal usage preference, not a manufacturer storage-charge specification.")
#para("Use the intended external supply. A full-looking battery may still need the plunger or a brief power connection before startup, as Chapter 1 describes. Bag charging requires the foam alignment. The battery display can indicate charging from the wireless receiver, but is hidden while the computer is packed in the bag. A USB power monitor can show power drawn by the bag charger; it does not directly measure what reaches the battery. Chapter 1 explains this limitation.")
]
#block(breakable:false)[
#heading(level:2,"Stand, bag and transport")
#para("Put the folding stand on a solid flat table, open it securely, and center the PiForma. The stand may permit some side-to-side motion, so keep it away from bumps and do not use it on an unstable surface.")
#para("Pack in the exact order in Chapter 1. Seat the computer in the bottom foam indents, orient the keyboard correctly, and replace the protective board before the pad, guide, mouse/stand, and pouch. The bag’s padding helps; it does not justify dropping it.")
]
#block(breakable:false)[
#heading(level:2,"Bose speakers and stands")
#para("Move the speakers and stands carefully and keep their cables from pulling on the computer. Do not assume the stands can be carried by the speakers or folded while attached.")
]
#block(breakable:false)[
#heading(level:2,"Cleaning, ventilation and unusual behavior")
#para("Switch off and disconnect charging power before ordinary exterior cleaning. Use a soft dry cloth gently on the case; keep liquids and solvents away from openings and internal parts. Confirm the LCD’s cleaning instructions before using a screen-cleaning product.")
#para("Leave vents clear and watch for unusual heat, smell, swelling, damaged wiring, or electrical behavior that is out of character. Stop using the machine in that condition. The build’s heat history is a reason to investigate, not to ignore a problem because the desktop still appears.")
]
#block(breakable:false)[
#heading(level:2,"Service and support")
#para("There isn’t any. Sorry.")
#para("The Macintosh PiForma is a one-off project made for enjoyment, not manufacture or sale. There is no service department, warranty desk, or helpful person in a tie waiting by the phone. If it needs repair, it will probably return to the person who built it, assuming he is in the mood.")
#para("That does not make unusual heat or electrical damage a joke. Stop using an unsafe-looking machine and speak to the builder rather than continuing to experiment. Treat it kindly and perhaps neither of us will have to find out how extensive the service department’s paperwork is.")
